# Keep dev-only files out of the deployed Vercel Python function bundle.
# What ships: app/, api/, migrations/, alembic.ini, pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, requirements.txt. Everything below is tests, load/dev tooling,
# caches, or local env — never imported by the request path.
#
# Note requirements.txt ships but is not the install manifest: Vercel
# resolves dependencies from pyproject.toml + uv.lock (docs/DEPLOY.md).
# It is kept as the pip-audit input and a readable record of the closure.

tests/
loadtest/
tools/

**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# Local env files are never git-committed, but exclude them defensively so a
# `vercel deploy` from the working tree can't upload them. Keep the example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
